# Environment for the Prefect worker process. Every worker unit reads it from
# hub-pipelines/prefect/worker.env, which is ONE DIRECTORY UP from this example: the units set
# EnvironmentFile=@PREFECT_DIR@/worker.env, and PREFECT_DIR is prefect/, not prefect/workers/.
# So copying this file in place leaves it where nothing reads it. Copy it to
# hub-pipelines/prefect/worker.env, or let workers/hpc/bootstrap.sh write that file for you.
# It is gitignored at any depth because a worker env has historically held credentials.
#
# It holds none now. A composed lamindb connection URL used to be here, described as feeding flow parameter
# validators that query LaminDB. No such reader was ever written, in this repo or in
# clinicalomx_pipeline, so the line only published the Postgres superuser credential to a file
# on the VM. Anything that does need the instance goes through lamindb, which asks LaminHub
# which database the instance is. See docs/runbooks/lamindb-connection.md.
#
# PREFECT_API_URL: the local Prefect server the worker connects to.
# MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI: the LOCAL MLflow this host's own workers use. It must not be the
#   floating IP: a process on the VM cannot reach the VM's own floating IP because Nectar
#   does not hairpin it, so a VM-side flow using the external address times out.
#
# The EXTERNAL addresses HPC jobs report back to, PREFECT_EXTERNAL_API_URL and
# MLFLOW_EXTERNAL_TRACKING_URI, are not here: they are site values, derived from
# hub.public_address in site.yaml and written to the repository root's site.env by
# scripts/site/render.py. The HPC worker units read that file as a second EnvironmentFile.
PREFECT_API_URL=http://localhost:4200/api
MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=http://localhost:5000
